# Trivy ignore file — accepted-risk vulnerabilities in the spc-bot image.
#
# Policy: the release gate fails on NEW FIXABLE CRITICAL/HIGH (scan with
# --ignore-unfixed --severity CRITICAL,HIGH --exit-code 1). The entries
# below are either CVEs with NO FIX AVAILABLE in the Debian trixie package
# pool as of 2026-08-14, or build-layer ghosts verified absent from the
# final runtime filesystem. Accepted risk for one of these reasons:
#
#   1. MEDIA CODEC / render-path libs the bot does not exercise at
#      runtime (matplotlib/cartopy render plots; the bot never decodes
#      untrusted H.265/HEIF/TIFF/AVIF streams).
#   2. TRANSITIVE deps of the geo stack (libgdal36's optional MariaDB
#      driver, libssh2, gnupg/dirmngr) that nothing in the bot calls.
#   3. PENDING DEBIAN: the fix exists upstream but trixie has not
#      shipped a patched package yet. These clear via apt-get upgrade
#      on the next image rebuild; re-check periodically and remove from
#      this file once Debian publishes the fix.
#   4. BUILD-LAYER GHOST (verified 2026-08-14): present in the wheel
#      COPY layer (FROM builder /build/wheels) but NOT importable in
#      the final image (pip show/import both fail). The wheels dir is
#      rm'd at runtime; only the layer history carries the files.
#
# Re-check cadence: run `trivy image ghcr.io/full-bars/spc-bot:<tag>`
# before each release; remove entries whose CVE now has a FixedVersion.

# --- Build-layer ghosts: verified not present in final runtime image ---
CVE-2025-47273   # setuptools 70.3.0 in wheel COPY layer; not importable
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 # msgpack 1.1.2 in wheel COPY layer; not importable

# --- Media codec / render path (not exercised by the bot) ---
CVE-2026-33164   # libde265: H.265 video codec
CVE-2026-36849   # libtiff6: DoS via SamplesPerPixel (TIFF decoding)
CVE-2026-41992   # gzip: LZH decompression (no untrusted gzip input path)

# --- Transitive deps of the geo stack (unused at runtime) ---
CVE-2026-44168   # mariadb-common: gdal's optional MariaDB driver
CVE-2026-44171   # mariadb-common: mbstream path traversal
CVE-2026-44172   # mariadb-common: SQL injection
CVE-2026-48163   # mariadb-common: parameter validation
CVE-2026-48165   # mariadb-common: global system variable
CVE-2026-49261   # mariadb-common: wsrep_notify_cmd
CVE-2026-49014   # libgdal36: netCDF container parsing
CVE-2026-8086    # libgdal36: OSGeo gdal
CVE-2026-8087    # libgdal36: OSGeo gdal
CVE-2026-58050   # libssh2: heap overflow (bot does not use SSH)
CVE-2026-24882   # gpgsm (gnupg): tpm2daemon stack overflow (no GPG use)
CVE-2026-54369   # libacl1: symlink traversal (no acl-tooling use)
CVE-2026-53615   # util-linux: libblkid integer overflow (boot-time tool)

# --- Core libs, pending Debian trixie security updates ---
CVE-2026-12064   # libcurl4t64: SSH host verification (schemeless URLs)
CVE-2026-8286    # libcurl4t64: TLS configuration
CVE-2026-8458    # libcurl4t64: connection reuse
CVE-2026-8927    # libcurl4t64: proxy auth state leak
CVE-2026-69720   # ncurses-bin: buffer overflow
CVE-2026-57432   # perl-base: integer overflow in pack/unpack
CVE-2026-42497   # perl-base: Archive-Tar arbitrary file modification
CVE-2026-48962   # perl-base: IO-Compress arbitrary code execution
CVE-2026-9538    # perl-base: Archive-Tar DoS
CVE-2026-13221   # perl-base: regex silent incorrect results
CVE-2026-42496   # perl-base: Archive-Tar path traversal
CVE-2026-57433   # perl-base: Storable integer overflow
CVE-2026-8376    # perl-base: regex heap overflow
CVE-2026-6653    # libxml2: DoS via crafted XML (mingw variant)
